I'll give you a practical, step-by-step proof of concept for your existing AWS RES Ubuntu Workbench, using Windows mstsc.exe and without installing XRDP.

The steps below use GNOME Remote Desktop's Remote Login mode, which is more suitable for a cloud Workbench than ordinary desktop sharing because it can provide a login screen without requiring an already active desktop session. GNOME documents this mode for RDP, with GDM managing the graphical login. 
