Before starting: confirm the Ubuntu version. The configuration differs substantially between Ubuntu releases, and the GNOME Remote Desktop package must support Remote Login mode.
Step 1 — Check the existing Workbench
Connect through your existing SSH or SSM method and run:
cat /etc/os-release
echo "Desktop: $XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP"
echo "Session: $XDG_SESSION_TYPE"

dpkg -l | grep -E 'gnome-shell|gdm3|gnome-remote-desktop|ubuntu-desktop'


Also check whether XRDP is already installed and whether port 3389 is in use:
dpkg -l | grep xrdp
sudo ss -lntp | grep ':3389'


Save the output. Do not remove or stop any existing service yet.
Step 2 — Confirm the Ubuntu version supports your intended setup
The distinction is important:
- Ubuntu 24.04 LTS or later with GNOME: proceed with the Remote Login proof of concept.
- Ubuntu 22.04 LTS: do not assume the built-in GNOME RDP server supports the headless Remote Login configuration you need. Its documented RDP functionality is different. 
