Important correction for Ubuntu 22.04
The official Ubuntu remote-desktop test plan confirms that Remote Login using GNOME's system-level RDP service is supported on Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and later, not Ubuntu 22.04 LTS. Ubuntu 22.04's GNOME 42 supports RDP for sharing an existing desktop, which is a different mode. 
Ubuntu project documentation+1


Therefore, the earlier grdctl --system steps should not be applied to your Ubuntu 22.04 Workbench as if they were supported. Installing gnome-remote-desktop on 22.04 does not automatically provide the system-level Remote Login functionality you need.

For your requirements, I recommend this safe path:
1. Inspect the existing Ubuntu 22.04 Workbench without changing it.
2. If you require system-level GNOME Remote Login, test it on a separate Ubuntu 24.04 LTS clone or test Workbench.
3. Preserve the existing RES, AD/SSSD, DCV and SSM configuration while validating the new desktop access method.
Step 1 — Inspect your Ubuntu 22.04 Workbench
Run these commands through SSM or SSH. They are read-only and will not modify the Workbench.
